1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,581
Christmas, five days, leaving from Paris.

2
00:00:03,631 --> 00:00:08,066
I asked Google one question: where can
I go for the least money?

3
00:00:08,116 --> 00:00:10,840
And the map gave me an answer
I didn't expect.

4
00:00:11,090 --> 00:00:12,422
Manchester.

5
00:00:12,472 --> 00:00:18,110
Sixty-six euros return, non-stop, an
hour and twenty minutes.

6
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:22,335
One small trap: it leaves from
Beauvais, with no cabin bag.

7
00:00:22,385 --> 00:00:24,520
From Charles de Gaulle, it's ninety-two.

8
00:00:24,770 --> 00:00:27,444
So I built three trips to the same city.

9
00:00:27,494 --> 00:00:30,140
And for each one, a different method.

10
00:00:30,390 --> 00:00:33,937
Trip one: solo, under five hundred euros.

11
00:00:33,987 --> 00:00:39,007
Method: I sort everything by price, and
only keep ratings above eight.

12
00:00:39,057 --> 00:00:43,816
A room rated eight point six, two hundred and
twenty-eight euros for five nights.

13
00:00:43,866 --> 00:00:46,396
With the flight, I'm under three hundred.

14
00:00:46,446 --> 00:00:49,102
That leaves two hundred to
eat and explore.

15
00:00:49,350 --> 00:00:52,377
Trip two: a couple, one thousand euros.

16
00:00:52,427 --> 00:00:54,833
This time, I didn't search
anything myself.

17
00:00:54,883 --> 00:00:58,985
I asked an AI for everything in one
sentence: flights, hotel,

18
00:00:59,035 --> 00:01:01,299
halal restaurants with no alcohol,

19
00:01:01,349 --> 00:01:04,703
and one activity a day that's
open on those dates.

20
00:01:04,950 --> 00:01:07,327
And that's where it surprised me.

21
00:01:07,377 --> 00:01:09,545
It checked the holiday opening hours.

22
00:01:09,595 --> 00:01:18,294
It steered me away from a library that was
closed for the whole holiday last year.

23
00:01:18,344 --> 00:01:21,872
And according to it, the stadium tour lands
on the only day with no match.

24
00:01:22,130 --> 00:01:24,843
Total: nine hundred and
fifty-five euros for two.

25
00:01:24,893 --> 00:01:29,275
But careful: it admits its own hotel and
flight prices are estimates.

26
00:01:29,325 --> 00:01:31,668
So you check the prices on the real sites.

27
00:01:31,910 --> 00:01:36,645
Trip three: a family of four, two
thousand five hundred euros.

28
00:01:36,695 --> 00:01:38,523
Method: the map.

29
00:01:38,573 --> 00:01:41,496
I look for halal restaurants
around the centre,

30
00:01:41,546 --> 00:01:43,963
and pick the hotel right in the middle.

31
00:01:44,013 --> 00:01:46,955
An apartment with a kitchen,
rated nine point two,

32
00:01:47,005 --> 00:01:49,708
four hundred and fifty metres
from the centre.

33
00:01:49,758 --> 00:01:54,371
One thousand and fifty-nine euros for five
nights, and the kids stay free.

34
00:01:54,620 --> 00:01:56,935
Flights for four, the apartment,

35
00:01:56,985 --> 00:02:01,518
and there's about a thousand euros
left for meals and outings.

36
00:02:01,568 --> 00:02:04,530
The science museum and the
Manchester Museum are free.

37
00:02:04,780 --> 00:02:06,352
One detail nobody looks at:

38
00:02:06,402 --> 00:02:11,096
Google tells me that leaving on the
twenty-seventh instead of the twenty-sixth,

39
00:02:11,146 --> 00:02:13,259
the flight drops to forty-one euros.

40
00:02:13,309 --> 00:02:17,911
One day later, and the cheapest
trip gets even cheaper.

41
00:02:17,961 --> 00:02:20,751
And you, where would you go with
five hundred euros?

